    "intro_html":  "Cumin beef out of Xinjiang is what happens when Central Asian spice meets a Chinese wok. Thin sliced beef gets a cornstarch coating so it stays tender, then hits screaming heat with a heavy pour of cumin and chili flakes. Total cook time is under half an hour once the slicing is done. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and {{cal}} calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
